# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
main.js
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vault content must NEVER be committed. This repo is PUBLIC and holds source
# code only. `test-vault/` is the sole exception: it is synthetic by rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/vault/
*.vault/
**/95 Exports/
**/82 Audit/
**/80 Time/
**/75 Correspondence/
**/94 Runs/

# The one narrowing of the rule above, and only this one.
#
# `75 Correspondence/` is blanket-ignored because §5.10 permits full message
# bodies and attachments there — it is the highest-risk folder in a real vault.
# But the synthetic threads in `test-vault/` document that contract the same way
# the synthetic requests document §5.1, and the fixture tests assert on them, so
# a fresh clone without them fails. They are covered by the same guard as every
# other fixture: `tests/fixtures.test.ts` refuses any address outside RFC 2606's
# reserved example domains, and refuses a `body` key on any message.
#
# `82 Audit/`, `80 Time/`, `95 Exports/` and `94 Runs/` stay ignored even under
# test-vault: those are generated output, not contract documentation.
!/test-vault/75 Correspondence/

# Obsidian per-machine state (never useful in the repo)
**/.obsidian/workspace*
**/.obsidian/plugins/scdb-cockpit/
**/.obsidian/cache

# Machine-local secrets: absolute paths and git identity. Never committed.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Generated by "Create Bases dashboards". Output, not fixture: committing them
# would make a fresh clone hit the already-exists path instead of the one that
# actually needs testing.
**/90 Dashboards/*.base

# Same argument for the daily briefing: it is a dated record the plugin writes,
# not a worked example of the contract. Committing one would also mean a test
# run in the test vault dirties the tree every morning.
**/90 Dashboards/Briefings/
